{"type": "message", "id": "324490a0", "parentId": "eb3e5dce", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T05:46:53.379Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_G7PxvcH09RxsxUlmqHxmfYpj", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"\\\"Kentucky\\\" \\\"NAEP\\\" \\\"Grade 8\\\" math 2022 average score Kentucky 8th grade math 2022 NAEP score\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 3,\n  \"tookMs\": 850,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"81654e7e8135d176\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KENTUCKY  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"81654e7e8135d176\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KY8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d073a9fba4b5c239\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d073a9fba4b5c239\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8b0e29fbd7f9e9cd\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOVEMBER 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8b0e29fbd7f9e9cd\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://csgsouth.org/wp-content/uploads/QofM-November.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f42cd5f6ce18849f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nProcess (NAEP). 2022 Mathematics Assessment.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f42cd5f6ce18849f\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"csgsouth.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"49971133c82a1433\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nKentucky Shows Promise with Post-COVID Test Scores – Prichard Committee for Academic Excellence\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"49971133c82a1433\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://prichardcommittee.org/kentucky-shows-promise-with-post-covid-test-scores/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"86fc07826cf870a0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn percent of students reaching NAEP proficiency or above, Kentucky’s newest results are statistically tied with the nation in grade 4 reading, grade 8 reading and grade 4 math, with results below the nation in grade 8 math. Kentucky’s 4th-grade math results showed statistically significant improvement compared to 2022. Kentucky’s results in 4th-grade reading and 8th-grade math and reading remained steady for percent proficient or above, which makes it the first year the commonwealth has stopped the backward slide that began prior to COVID-19 and was further exacerbated by the pandemic.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"86fc07826cf870a0\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 29, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"prichardcommittee.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "\"Kentucky\" \"NAEP\" \"Grade 8\" math 2022 average score Kentucky 8th grade math 2022 NAEP score", "provider": "brave", "count": 3, "tookMs": 850, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"81654e7e8135d176\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KENTUCKY  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"81654e7e8135d176\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KY8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d073a9fba4b5c239\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d073a9fba4b5c239\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8b0e29fbd7f9e9cd\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOVEMBER 2022\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8b0e29fbd7f9e9cd\">>>", "url": "https://csgsouth.org/wp-content/uploads/QofM-November.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f42cd5f6ce18849f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nProcess (NAEP). 2022 Mathematics Assessment.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f42cd5f6ce18849f\">>>", "siteName": "csgsouth.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"49971133c82a1433\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nKentucky Shows Promise with Post-COVID Test Scores – Prichard Committee for Academic Excellence\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"49971133c82a1433\">>>", "url": "https://prichardcommittee.org/kentucky-shows-promise-with-post-covid-test-scores/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"86fc07826cf870a0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn percent of students reaching NAEP proficiency or above, Kentucky’s newest results are statistically tied with the nation in grade 4 reading, grade 8 reading and grade 4 math, with results below the nation in grade 8 math. Kentucky’s 4th-grade math results showed statistically significant improvement compared to 2022. Kentucky’s results in 4th-grade reading and 8th-grade math and reading remained steady for percent proficient or above, which makes it the first year the commonwealth has stopped the backward slide that began prior to COVID-19 and was further exacerbated by the pandemic.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"86fc07826cf870a0\">>>", "published": "January 29, 2025", "siteName": "prichardcommittee.org"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775281613378}}
